## Conventions (read by the workflow)

- **query_library**: `@tanstack/react-query` | `swr` | `pinia` | `ngrx` | …
- **http_client**: `yourHttpClient()` | `axios` | `fetch`
- **response_transform**: `transformResponse(data)` | `toCamelCase` | `keysToCamelCase`
- **import_alias**: `@src/` | `@app/` | `~`
- **shared_components_path**: `src/generic/` | `src/shared/` | `src/common/`
- **i18n_pattern**: `defineMessages` + `useIntl` | `i18next`
- **branch**: <default base branch, e.g. `develop`>
- **commit_format**: e.g. `[JIRA-ID] type: description`

## Workflow Overrides (optional — repo-specific HARD-RULE knobs)

> Leave these OUT unless you need them. When absent, the kit uses generic-safe fallbacks
> (e.g. HARD RULE 23's endpoint_base_override stays INACTIVE; URL prefixes come from
> grepping `src/**/api.ts`). Only define them to pin repo-specific behavior.

- **reference_feature**: `src/<folder>/` — mirror naming conventions from here (HR29)
- **endpoint_base_override**: `/api/v1/.../` — REST base for a specific feature family (HR23)
- **api_url_convention**: canonical `/api/vN/` prefix + id-param names (HR20)
- **spec_section_map**: which spec sections hold Objectives / Components / AC (HR21/HR22)
- **ui_library**: component lib for selector pitfalls (e.g. `@your-org/ui-lib`)
